# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Abrar Faiyad et al. (2026). Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials Enable Molecular Dynamics Simulations of Doped MoS 2.
#   Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation. doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.5c02004  arXiv:2510.05339v4
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2510.05339v4 (sha256 8e9d7aa351f6c475...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 341 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/faiyad2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the pretrained UMA small (uma-sm-1p1) and UMA medium
# (uma-m-1p1), OMat task, evaluated on neutral formation energies of 25
# dopants at three sites in 48-atom MoS2 cells against fixed-cell
# Quantum ESPRESSO PBE relaxations (Zhang-Northrup formalism), and UMA
# small in ~3,100-atom heating-cooling MD. Formation-energy MAEs are
# encoded as energy MAEs on external evaluation data, as in earlier
# papers; nearest-neighbour distance errors, densities and mobilities are
# properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
