###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Relaxation and formation-energy calculation of the 48-atom systems for all 25 dopants took 0.53-0.97 h with UMA small and 0.6-1.2 h with UMA medium (Nvidia A100 or L40), against about 410 h with DFT on 56 CPU cores (Methods). UMA small is about twice as fast as UMA medium in steps per second.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The compute times are ranges over a whole workflow and two GPU types, not per-structure timings, so they are kept in resources only.
# - Pearson r and R2 (>0.9), per-dopant cumulative errors (Fig. 4, S1) and nearest-neighbour distance errors (Fig. 5) are figure-only or properties.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/faiyad2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

